{
  "__comment": "Carved wall plaque, PORTRAIT: narrower across and taller up than the original square plate, so the sunken well can carry a readable sheet rather than a token. Built from real depth rather than a picture on a slab: an oak backboard, four forged-iron corner brackets standing proud of it, a raised aged-brass inner frame, the plan panel sunk behind that frame, and a status lamp in the gap between the lower brackets. Every element was reshaped by one proportional mapping, so the ironwork, brass and lamp stay in register. Modelled facing NORTH; the blockstate rotates it. Depth runs z=16 (against the wall) outward to z=11.6.",
